#! ia 1.0

@agent product-steward
  meaning
    says "Maintains product identity, closed structural schema and the public product authoring reference."
    answers "Who owns the product word and its structural contract without granting service authority?"
  governance
    applies [product]
    requires
      - "Read system.ia, schemas/product.schema.ia, schemas/product.SPEC.md and the distribution SPEC before changes."
      - "Preserve the sole product-system owner, exact format contract and typed owner/plan references; never add computed readiness or implicit permissions."
      - "Qualify actual emitted before/after adoption, product-reader success and structural/reference refusals; syntax alone is not readiness."
      - "Native admission only checks numeric format type and may warn about dangling refs; the product reader must enforce format 1 and resolve owner/plans."
      - "Keep service mappings, retirement effects and provider authority in their private API owner; never infer them from this authored owner."
      - "Maintain schema, guide, authoring/architecture references, consumer and refusal cases together; record exact release evidence and remaining limitations."
